- name: vibrate
  type: table
  desc: Cross-platform vibration and haptic feedback for Android, iOS, and HTML5.
        The module is also registered on unsupported platforms, where capability
        checks return false and playback calls fail gracefully.
  members:

    - name: trigger
      type: function
      desc: Play a vibration or haptic effect.
            Options are resolved in this order on the active platform,
            platform-specific mode/payload, common pattern, preset, then
            duration/default. Invalid option types, ranges, or combinations raise
            a Lua error. Runtime failures are returned as `false, reason`.
      parameters:
        - name: options
          type: table|nil
          desc: Optional effect description. Passing nil, or omitting this argument,
                requests the native default effect, with a 1000 ms timed fallback.
          members:
            - name: duration_ms
              type: number
              desc: Fallback one-shot duration in integer milliseconds, from 0 to 3600000.

            - name: intensity
              type: number
              desc: Common intensity from 0 to 1. Defaults to 1. Unsupported platforms
                    approximate or ignore it.

            - name: sharpness
              type: number
              desc: Common sharpness from 0 to 1. Defaults to 0.5 and is primarily
                    meaningful for iOS Core Haptics.

            - name: fallback
              type: boolean
              desc: Allow a less capable effect when the requested platform feature is
                    unavailable. Defaults to true.

            - name: preset
              type: string
              desc: Semantic preset. One of `default`, `selection`, `impact_light`,
                    `impact_medium`, `impact_heavy`, `impact_soft`, `impact_rigid`,
                    `success`, `warning`, `error`, `click`, `double_click`, `tick`,
                    or `heavy_click`.

            - name: pattern
              type: table
              desc: Array of 1 to 256 integer durations in milliseconds. Entries
                    alternate vibration and pause, beginning with vibration.

            - name: intensities
              type: table
              desc: Optional 0..1 intensity for every common pattern entry. Its length
                    must equal `pattern`; values in pause entries are ignored.

            - name: sharpnesses
              type: table
              desc: Optional 0..1 sharpness for every common pattern entry. Its length
                    must equal `pattern`; values in pause entries are ignored.

            - name: android
              type: table
              desc: Android-only override.
              members:
                - name: mode
                  type: string
                  desc: One of `auto`, `one_shot`, `waveform`, `predefined`, or
                        `composition`.
                - name: amplitude
                  type: number
                  desc: One-shot amplitude. Use -1 for the device default, or an integer
                        from 0 to 255.
                - name: effect
                  type: string
                  desc: Predefined effect; `click`, `double_click`, `tick`, or
                        `heavy_click`.
                - name: usage
                  type: string
                  desc: Vibration usage; `touch`, `game`, `notification`, `alarm`, or
                        `media`.
                - name: timings
                  type: table
                  desc: Raw waveform segment durations in integer milliseconds.
                - name: amplitudes
                  type: table
                  desc: Raw waveform amplitude per timing entry. Each value is -1 or
                        an integer from 0 to 255. When both arrays are present, their
                        lengths must match.
                - name: repeat_index
                  type: number
                  desc: -1 for no repeat, or a positive 1-based Lua index into
                        `android.timings`, or the common `pattern` when raw timings
                        are omitted. Repeating effects continue until
                        `vibrate.cancel()`.
                - name: primitives
                  type: table
                  desc: Android composition entries. Each item is a table with `name`,
                        optional `scale`, and optional `delay_ms`.

            - name: ios
              type: table
              desc: iOS-only override.
              members:
                - name: mode
                  type: string
                  desc: One of `auto`, `system`, `selection`, `impact`, `notification`,
                        or `core_haptics`.
                - name: style
                  type: string
                  desc: Impact style; `light`, `medium`, `heavy`, `soft`, or `rigid`.
                - name: notification
                  type: string
                  desc: Notification type; `success`, `warning`, or `error`.
                - name: repeat
                  type: boolean
                  desc: Repeat a Core Haptics pattern until `vibrate.cancel()`.
                - name: events
                  type: table
                  desc: Core Haptics event array. Each event accepts `type`
                        (`transient` or `continuous`), `time_ms`, `duration_ms`,
                        `intensity`, and `sharpness`. Continuous events require
                        `duration_ms > 0`.
                - name: ahap_json
                  type: string
                  desc: Raw AHAP JSON for Core Haptics. Mutually exclusive with
                        `ios.events`.

            - name: web
              type: table
              desc: HTML5-only override.
              members:
                - name: pattern
                  type: table
                  desc: Web Vibration API pattern with alternating vibration/pause durations
                        beginning with vibration.
                - name: duration_ms
                  type: number
                  desc: Web-only one-shot duration in integer milliseconds.
      returns:
        - name: success
          type: boolean
          desc: True when the active platform accepted the request.
        - name: reason
          type: string|nil
          desc: Nil on success; otherwise `unsupported`, `not_allowed`, `not_visible`,
                `rejected`, `no_hardware`, or `platform_error`.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            local ok, reason = vibrate.trigger({
                preset = "impact_medium",
                intensity = 0.8,
                web = { pattern = { 30, 20, 50 } },
            })
            if not ok then
                print("Haptics unavailable:", reason)
            end
            ```

    - name: cancel
      type: function
      desc: Cancel the currently repeating or cancellable effect. UIKit one-shot
            feedback cannot be cancelled after it has been emitted.
      returns:
        - name: success
          type: boolean
          desc: True when cancellation was accepted.
        - name: reason
          type: string|nil
          desc: Nil on success, otherwise a runtime failure reason.

    - name: is_supported
      type: function
      desc: Check whether the current device and platform expose vibration or haptics.
      returns:
        - name: supported
          type: boolean

    - name: get_capabilities
      type: function
      desc: Return the active platform's runtime capabilities. Capability values can
            vary by OS version, browser, and physical device.
      returns:
        - name: capabilities
          type: table
          desc: A table containing `platform`, `supported`, `pattern`, `intensity`,
                `sharpness`, `cancel`, `predefined`, `composition`, `repeat`,
                `core_haptics`, and `user_activation_required`.
